      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was incorporated on October 7, 1903, and today spans roughly 0.48 square miles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/elliott_illinois",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Construction of the Lafayette, Bloomington and Mississippi Railroad between 1870 and 1872 sparked Elliott’s early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/elliott_illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ford County, where Elliott lies, was organized in 1859 from Vermillion County after draining swampy prairies into productive farmland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/elliott_illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Elliott’s post office opened in 1871, serving the rural community for over a century.",
